DJMemory is a native macOS utility that automatically archives DJ set recordings from Serato DJ Pro,
rekordbox, Traktor, VirtualDJ, and djay Pro. SwiftUI, macOS 15+, SwiftPM tools 5.10, **no external
dependencies**.

## Specs

`HANDOFF.md` is the authoritative design spec: §2 tokens, §3 prototype→Swift type mapping and gaps
G1–G6, §4.1–§4.8 screens, §5 state matrix, §6 tasks, §7 non-negotiables.
`HANDOFF-2-HOME.md` adds §4.9 (Home dashboard), §4.10 (sidebar sources + add-app picker), gaps
G7–G9, and tasks T12–T13. Both are current. Read the relevant sections before writing UI.

The design prototype these specs describe is **not** checked out here. Prototype filenames in the
specs are provenance notes, not files you can open. If something is genuinely ambiguous, say so
rather than inventing a layout.

## Commands

- `swift build` / `swift test`
- `swift run DJMemoryApp`
- `swift run djmemory probe|scan|watch|virtualdj-network`
- `bash scripts/build-app.sh`, `bash scripts/smoke-app.sh`

You cannot launch and observe the macOS UI in a headless environment. Verification is builds, tests,
and `#Preview` coverage. Never claim a screen looks correct on that basis.

## Architecture

- `AppModel` is the only view model. `@MainActor ObservableObject`, state as `@Published
  private(set)`, mutated through methods. Do not add sibling view models or move state into views.
- `DJMemoryCore` stays UI-agnostic — no SwiftUI import, no `Color`.
- New fields on `Codable` models need defaults so existing stores keep decoding.
- Check whether a field already exists before adding a model. `ArchiveMetadata.durationSeconds` and
  `.fileSize` in particular already exist.

## Product commitments

These are commitments, not preferences. If a task appears to require breaking one, the task is wrong
— stop and say so.

1. Local-first.
2. Audio files are never uploaded by default.
3. Full tracklists are never uploaded by default.
4. Admins cannot access user audio or full tracklists.
5. Diagnostics exports contain metadata only.
6. Source recordings are never moved, renamed, or deleted — DJMemory copies.
7. Support labels are honest. "Partial" stays "Partial"; never round up to "Supported".
8. No dead ends. Every failure state names a cause and offers an action.

## Copy

Strings in the specs are load-bearing and often carry commitment 8 (a failure message that also says
what is still safe). Copy them verbatim. Do not paraphrase, shorten, or make them friendlier.

## Scope

One task per session, surgical edits. Do not rewrite a whole file to make a local change. Never
rename or remove an existing `accessibilityIdentifier`. Show your plan before editing more than one
view.
